      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-17",
      "revision": 1170023813,
      "text": "Begonia hirtella, the bearded begonia, is a species of flowering plant in the family Begoniaceae. It is native to Jamaica, Venezuela, Colombia, Peru, Bolivia, and southern Brazil, and has been introduced to many tropical locales around the world. People apply its juices to their skin to treat itchiness from insect bites."
    },
    "fr": {
      "source": "Wikipedia (fr): Begonia hirtella",
      "source_url": "https://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Begonia_hirtella",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-17",
      "revision": 203193141,
      "text": "Begonia hirtella est une espèce de plantes de la famille des Begoniaceae. Ce bégonia est originaire d'Amérique du Sud et des Caraïbes. L'espèce fait partie de la section Ephemera. Elle a été décrite en 1822 par Heinrich Friedrich Link (1767-1851). L'épithète spécifique hirtella signifie « plutôt hirsute », c'est-à-dire modérément garnie de poils raides et épais."
    },
    "pt": {
      "source": "Wikipedia (pt): Begonia hirtella",
      "source_url": "https://pt.wikipedia.org/wiki/Begonia_hirtella",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-17",
      "revision": 64457477,
      "text": "Begonia hirtella é uma espécie de planta do grupo Begonia decrita em 1822 por Heinrich Friedrich Link. É nativa, mas não endêmica, do Brasil."
    },
    "id": {
      "source": "Wikipedia (id): Begonia hirtella",
